-- title:
--   Specialisation of T_ℓ on divisors: Eichler–Shimura relation
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, and write $\bar F_M$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar M`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M$ modular function field inside Laurent series. Assume the two degeneracy maps $\alpha=$ `heckeAlphaBar` (the inclusion $\bar F_N\subseteq\bar F_{N\ell}$) and $\beta=$ `heckeBetaBar` (induced by the $q\mapsto q^\ell$ substitution) are integral ring homomorphisms, that $\bar F_{N\ell}$ has principal divisors over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (every nonzero function is the divisor, of degree $0$, of its orders at all places), and that every place $W$ of $\bar F_{N\ell}$ has degree $1$, i.e. residue field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-rank $1$. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\ell$, let `data` consist of a monic $\Phi\in\mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(\ell)$ vanishing at $(j,j_\ell)$, and let `hKr` assert that $\Phi$ mod $\ell$ equals $(C X^\ell-X)(C X-X^\ell)$; write $\varphi=$ `frobOnPlacesGeomLevel` for the resulting Frobenius operation on places of $\tilde F_N=k(j,j_N)=$ `modularFunctionFieldC k N`. Let $\mathrm{sp}$ be any map from places of $\bar F_N$ to places of $\tilde F_N$ such that (d1) for every place $W$ of $\bar F_{N\ell}$, $\mathrm{sp}(W|_\alpha)=\varphi(\mathrm{sp}(W|_\beta))$ or $\varphi(\mathrm{sp}(W|_\alpha))=\mathrm{sp}(W|_\beta)$, where $W|_\alpha$, $W|_\beta$ denote the restrictions of $W$ along $\alpha$, $\beta$; and (d2) for every place $v$ of $\bar F_N$ with $\varphi^2(\mathrm{sp}(v))\ne \mathrm{sp}(v)$ there is a place $W_0$ of $\bar F_{N\ell}$ with $W_0|_\beta=v$, $\mathrm{sp}(W_0|_\alpha)=\varphi(\mathrm{sp}(v))$, ramification index $1$ over $v$ along $\beta$, and $W_0$ is the unique place above $v$ with $\mathrm{sp}(W|_\alpha)=\varphi(\mathrm{sp}(v))$. Then for every place $v$ of $\bar F_N$ the pushforward along $\mathrm{sp}$ of $T_\ell[v]=$ `heckeDivBar hα hβ` applied to the divisor $1\cdot v$ equals `heckeFibreGeomLevel`, the sum of the Frobenius pushforward and Frobenius pullback on divisors of $\tilde F_N$, applied to $1\cdot \mathrm{sp}(v)$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura congruence relation $T_\ell=F_*+F^*$ in its divisor-theoretic, place-by-place form: the geometric input is isolated in the two clauses (d1) and (d2) on the specialisation map $\mathrm{sp}$, and the statement converts them into the identity of divisors on the characteristic-$\ell$ curve. It is used in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.spPic0_heckeGen_ell_eq_heckeFibreGeom`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.spPic0_heckeGen_ell_eq_heckeFibreGeom) to transport the relation to degree-zero divisor classes.
